## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to wire basic observability across static web apps, serverless functions, and a database, a foundational skill for troubleshooting in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Application Insights integration on SPA and Function
- Correlation IDs across SPA -> Function -> SQL
- Log Analytics queries to join telemetry and database logs
- End-to-end request tracing and basic dashboards

## Code Example
```javascript
// SPA instrumentation and correlationId
import { ApplicationInsights } from "@microsoft/applicationinsights-web";
const appInsights = new ApplicationInsights({ config: { instrumentationKey: "<ikey>" } });
appInsights.loadAppInsights();
const correlationId = crypto.randomUUID();
fetch("/api/feedback", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "X-Correlation-Id": correlationId, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ text, rating })
});
```

```csharp
// Function: read header and insert into SQL with correlationId
string corr = req.Headers["X-Correlation-Id"];
using (var cmd = new SqlCommand("INSERT INTO Feedback (Text, CorrId) VALUES (@t, @c)", conn)) {
  cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@t", text);
  cmd.Parameters.AddWithValue("@c", corr);
  cmd.ExecuteNonQuery();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify the correlation path in Log Analytics?
- How would you handle missing correlation IDs in edge cases?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design a secure, scalable multi-tenant Azure solution with governance, cross-tenant admin, and IaC automation.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant data isolation using dedicated Azure SQL DBs with Row-Level Security
- Azure API Management as the single API surface and gateway
- Private endpoints and VNET integration to DBs
- Azure Lighthouse for cross-tenant administrative access with least-privilege RBAC
- Azure Policy for governance (tags, allowed SKUs, resource locks)
- Terraform + GitHub Actions for CI/CD; cost budgets and telemetry for observability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: validate that RLS is enabled for a tenant database (illustrative)
function validateTenantDB(config){
  if(!config.sql || !config.sql.rlsEnabled){
    throw new Error("RLS must be enabled per tenant database");
  }
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test policy compliance and Lighthouse configurations across subscriptions?
- How would you implement a safe rollback plan for Terraform changes that violate governance rules?

